    <title>Core Concepts</title>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="md_docs_2content_2getting__started_2core__concepts_1autotoc_md94"/> This page describes the primary data structures and representations used in HighMap.</para>
<sect1 id="md_docs_2content_2getting__started_2core__concepts_1autotoc_md95">
<title>1. Elevation Representations</title>
<para>HighMap provides three main structures for 2D height data:</para>
<para><table rows="4" cols="3"><row>
<entry thead="yes" align='left'><para>Structure   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes" align='left'><para>Type   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes" align='left'><para>Description    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='left'><para><computeroutput>Array</computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no" align='left'><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Array" kindref="compound">hmap::Array</ref></computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no" align='left'><para>In-memory 2D array of floats with contiguous storage.    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='left'><para><computeroutput>HeightMap</computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no" align='left'><para><computeroutput>hmap::HeightMap</computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no" align='left'><para>Tiled 2D array designed for parallel computation.    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no" align='left'><para><computeroutput>VirtualArray</computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no" align='left'><para><computeroutput><ref refid="structhmap_1_1VirtualArray" kindref="compound">hmap::VirtualArray</ref></computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no" align='left'><para>Tiled structure supporting disk and RAM storage for large grids.   </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<sect2 id="md_docs_2content_2getting__started_2core__concepts_1autotoc_md96">
<title>Array</title>
<para><computeroutput>Array</computeroutput> is the basic container for 2D elevation fields. Data is stored in row-major order. It supports arithmetic operators, statistical queries, slicing, and filtering.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Array" kindref="compound">hmap::Array</ref><sp/><ref refid="hydraulic__mise_8cpp_1aa14e04bff7de9e968e46a953f71f29f3" kindref="member">z</ref>({512,<sp/>512});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="hydraulic__mise_8cpp_1aa14e04bff7de9e968e46a953f71f29f3" kindref="member">z</ref><sp/>=<sp/>1.0f;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">float</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>val<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="hydraulic__mise_8cpp_1aa14e04bff7de9e968e46a953f71f29f3" kindref="member">z</ref>(<ref refid="sls__deformation_8cpp_1acb559820d9ca11295b4500f179ef6392" kindref="member">i</ref>,<sp/><ref refid="sls__deformation_8cpp_1a37d972ae0b47b9099e30983131d31916" kindref="member">j</ref>);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md_docs_2content_2getting__started_2core__concepts_1autotoc_md97">
<title>2. Bivariate Functions</title>
<para>Continuous functions deriving from <computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Function" kindref="compound">hmap::Function</ref></computeroutput> represent mathematical surfaces $f(x, y)$ independently of resolution:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1NoiseFunction" kindref="compound">hmap::NoiseFunction</ref></computeroutput>: Perlin, Simplex, and cellular noise generators.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1FbmFunction" kindref="compound">hmap::FbmFunction</ref></computeroutput>: Multi-octave fractal noise.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1FieldFunction" kindref="compound">hmap::FieldFunction</ref></computeroutput>: Distance fields and geometric functions.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md_docs_2content_2getting__started_2core__concepts_1autotoc_md98">
<title>3. Geometric Primitives</title>
<para>Geometric entities represent vector features and integrate with height arrays:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Point" kindref="compound">hmap::Point</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Cloud" kindref="compound">hmap::Cloud</ref></computeroutput>: Individual points and point clouds.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="structhmap_1_1Edge" kindref="compound">hmap::Edge</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Path" kindref="compound">hmap::Path</ref></computeroutput>: Segments and ordered sequences of points.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Graph" kindref="compound">hmap::Graph</ref></computeroutput>: Node and edge graphs used for networks such as rivers and roads.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md_docs_2content_2getting__started_2core__concepts_1autotoc_md99">
<title>4. Scattering</title>
<para>The scattering system handles the distribution of discrete objects over a terrain:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1ScatterItem" kindref="compound">hmap::ScatterItem</ref></computeroutput>: Basic element storing a 3D position, an integer class identifier, and a radius.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1ScatterField" kindref="compound">hmap::ScatterField</ref></computeroutput>: Container providing spatial operations (collision pruning, density maps, elevation projection).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1Forest" kindref="compound">hmap::Forest</ref></computeroutput>: Scattering container for vegetation and growth models.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classhmap_1_1RockField" kindref="compound">hmap::RockField</ref></computeroutput>: Scattering container for rock and debris placement. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect1>
